<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Altfrid</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 874</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Altfrid of Hildesheim</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Altfrid was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hildesheim">Hildesheim</a> from 851 until his death in 874 and is venerated as a saint. A churchman from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> nobility and an adviser to the East Frankish king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-the-german">Louis the German</a>, he founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/essen">Essen</a> Abbey as a community of canonesses around 845 to 852. He also built the first cathedral of Hildesheim, consecrated in 872.</p></div>
